{"diagnosis": "Loopback RX got 0xff (idle) instead of 0xa5 for divider 64. TX advances on line 130 with `send_divcnt > (cfg_divider >> 4)`, making the bit period ~16x too short, so TX finishes before RX samples and RX reads idle 1s. Root cause is the `>> 4` divide on cfg_divider in the send_bitcnt shift condition.", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picosoc/simpleuart.v b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
--- a/picosoc/simpleuart.v
+++ b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
@@ -125,9 +125,9 @@
 			if (reg_dat_we && !send_bitcnt) begin
 				send_pattern <= {1'b1, reg_dat_di[7:0], 1'b0};
 				send_bitcnt <= 10;
 				send_divcnt <= 0;
 			end else
-			if (send_divcnt > (cfg_divider >> 4) && send_bitcnt) begin
+			if (send_divcnt > cfg_divider && send_bitcnt) begin
 				send_pattern <= {1'b1, send_pattern[9:1]};
 				send_bitcnt <= send_bitcnt - 1;
 				send_divcnt <= 0;", "expected": "tohost: PASS (not FAIL 0xdead), TRAP uart data mismatch gone, log shows got 0xa5 want 0xa5; checksum changes from e251d79bc7250f734efe026d9d7f036e818ad243c9428000f5cdb2c1fd8b03c6"}

